SUMMARY:52nd Annual Houston Shakespeare Festival: The Comedy of Errors at Miller Outdoor Theatre
DESCRIPTION:Houston Shakespeare Festival\, the city’s annual summer theater tradition\, celebrates its 52nd season with performances of both The Tempest and The Comedy of Errors on alternating nights at Miller Outdoor Theatre. \nShakespeare’s Comedy of Errors\nShakespeare’s riotous farce of mistaken identity\, The Comedy of Errors\, brings double trouble to the bustling port city of Ephesus when two sets of twins—separated at birth—unexpectedly cross paths\, unleashing a whirlwind of mayhem and mirth. \nIn this fast-paced comedy bursting with physical humor\, outrageous confusion\, and joyful surprise\, husbands are mistaken for strangers\, servants are denied their own names\, and no one can tell friend from foe. As misunderstandings multiply and tempers flare\, the laughter never lets up. \nFinding Your Seat at Miller Outdoor Theatre\nAs always\, all seats at Miller are free\, but covered seating for popular evening shows usually requires a free assigned ticket reserved 24 hours in advance. \nLearn more about getting free seated tickets at Miller. \nAdmission\nFree. Learn more or reserve a free seated ticket. \n \nThis Featured Calendar Listing was sponsored by the event organizer and boosted in our calendar with images and more details.  \nLearn more about promoting your event\, organization\, business\, or offer across all of our channels.
URL:https://365thingsinhouston.com/calendar/52nd-annual-houston-shakespeare-festival-the-comedy-of-errors-at-miller-outdoor-theatre-1/
LOCATION:Miller Outdoor Theatre\, 6000 Hermann Park Dr\, Houston\, TX\, 77030\, United States
CATEGORIES:Arts Performances,Boosted Calendar Listing,Comedy,Date Night,Featured,Festivals,Free,History & Culture,Live Theater,Outdoors,Parks
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://365thingsinhouston.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/52nd-Annual-Houston-Shakespeare-Festival-The-Comedy-of-Errors-at-Miller-Outdoor-Theatre.jpeg
