SUMMARY:Road Trips Opening Reception at Archway Gallery
DESCRIPTION:Now celebrating its fiftieth year\, the member-owned Montrose gallery hosts a free opening reception for Road Trips\, an exhibit featuring new paintings by Lisette McClung. \nThis exhibit brings together a collection of both plein air and studio works—large and small—inspired by her many road trips over the past decade. \nPlein air—French for “open air”—refers to the practice of painting outdoors on location. As a dedicated plein air painter\, McClung has been invited to paint\, explore\, and photograph on a variety of working ranches\, as well as in fields\, cities\, and villages across the United States and Europe. \nThere will be an artist talk at 6:30pm. \nComplimentary valet parking and light refreshments available. \nThe exhibit will be on display from Saturday\, August 1 through Thursday\, September 3\, 2026. \nOpened in 1976\, Archway Gallery is currently celebrating its fiftieth year. \nAdmission\nFree. Learn more. If you visit Archway Gallery’s website before the exhibition opens\, be sure to click on “Exhibitions” in the top menu bar\, then on “Upcoming Exhibitions”\, to find details on this exhibit. \n“Running Wild” by Lisette McClung | Photos courtesy of Archway Gallery\n \nThis Featured Calendar Listing was sponsored by the event organizer and boosted in our calendar with images and more details. \nLearn more about promoting your event\, organization\, business\, or offer across all of our channels.
URL:https://365thingsinhouston.com/calendar/road-trips-opening-reception-at-archway-gallery/
LOCATION:Archway Gallery\, 2305 Dunlavy St\, Houston\, TX\, 77006\, United States
CATEGORIES:Art,Boosted Calendar Listing,Date Night,Featured,Free,Mixers,Receptions
