SUMMARY:52nd Annual Houston Shakespeare Festival: The Tempest at Miller Outdoor Theatre
DESCRIPTION:Houston Shakespeare Festival\, the city’s annual summer theater tradition\, celebrates its 52nd season with performances of both The Tempest and Comedy of Errors on alternating nights at Miller Outdoor Theatre. \nShakespeare’s The Tempest\nExiled by her brother to a remote island and left to die\, Prospera—the once loved Duchess of Milan and now an all-powerful sorceress—conjures a great tempest to wash ashore a ship of her enemies. \nWith the power of magic\, Prospera manipulates the survivors of the wreckage to weave a story of revenge\, retribution\, and reconciliation. Rich with spectacle\, humor and wonder\, Shakespeare’s final play brings audiences to a “brave new world ” where reconciliation is possible and humanity is renewed. \nFinding Your Seat at Miller Outdoor Theatre\nAs always\, all seats at Miller are free\, but covered seating for popular evening shows usually requires a free assigned ticket reserved 24 hours in advance. \nLearn more about getting free seated tickets at Miller. \nAdmission\nFree. Learn more or reserve a free seated ticket. \n \nThis Featured Calendar Listing was sponsored by the event organizer and boosted in our calendar with images and more details.  \nLearn more about promoting your event\, organization\, business\, or offer across all of our channels.
URL:https://365thingsinhouston.com/calendar/52nd-annual-houston-shakespeare-festival-the-tempest-at-miller-outdoor-theatre-2/
LOCATION:Miller Outdoor Theatre\, 6000 Hermann Park Dr\, Houston\, TX\, 77030\, United States
CATEGORIES:Arts Performances,Boosted Calendar Listing,Comedy,Date Night,Featured,Festivals,Free,History & Culture,Live Theater,Outdoors,Parks
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://365thingsinhouston.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/52nd-Annual-Houston-Shakespeare-Festival-The-Tempest-at-Miller-Outdoor-Theatre.jpeg
GEO:29.7191812;-95.3886681
